-- HTB deliberate change: audio and streaming re-weights (package 3 of the 2026-10-19 profile review).
--
-- Approved by Steven on 2026-10-19 (items B4, B9, B10, C1, C2, C9).
--   - C1 and C2: on the Quality and Remux profiles (2160p Quality, its Prefer Theatrical and English Dub
--     copies, 2160p Remux, its Prefer Theatrical copy, 2160p Remux Only, 1080p Quality, 720p Quality)
--     every lossless codec scores the same: TrueHD, DTS-HD MA, FLAC and PCM 2,000, DTS:X 2,010.
--     "TrueHD (Missing)" (an Atmos release that names no codec, assumed TrueHD) follows TrueHD.
--     Lossless then beats lossy from one release-group tier below, never two. Lossy is unchanged.
--     Balanced and Efficient are unchanged.
--   - B4: Atmos 400 (was 10) wherever these profiles already score an Atmos format. The 4K profiles
--     score "Atmos" and "Atmos (Missing)", the 1080p and 720p profiles "Dolby Atmos", as upstream.
--   - C9 and B10: streaming-service scores and the "Enhancement" adjustments become Dictionarry's
--     (fb09c84) in every profile. HTB-only profiles take their base profile's values.
--   - B9: Bravia Core +7,000 on the 4K Quality and Remux profiles. Its 0 elsewhere stays (upstream
--     bans it on 1080p, Balanced and Efficient; HTB doesn't).
--   - Upstream formats copied for C9: Discovery+ (DSCP), HBO and SkyShowtime (SKST), scored 0, and
--     the TV penalties Netflix Enhancement and Amazon Channel Enhancement. Where a pattern of the same
--     name already exists, HTB's pattern is kept; op 12 takes upstream's pattern fixes.

-- C1, C2, B4: audio.

-- C9, B10: upstream streaming values. B9: Bravia Core on the 4K Quality and Remux profiles.
